title modify/delete: onto deletes what off-of edited

# m1_smoke's conflict fixture, as a tree. Supplied by the kernel
# lane and validated against the reference before use: base 4 pools
# / 4 names, onto 4 / 4, off-of 4 / 5, one lineage conflict over 5
# components -- which matches what the real datasets produce, so the
# tree is faithful to the fixture rather than merely plausible.
#
# Used to cross-check the two independent emission compilers. The
# COUNT for this one was published before I ran it, so agreement on
# the count is confirmation rather than evidence; the edit LIST was
# not, and a difference there -- a different name, a different
# from=, a write on another pool -- would be a real finding the
# count could not have shown.

tree base
  1-1: /
    5-100: hello = hello-v0
    3-100: subdir/
      7-100: inner = inner-v0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    5-100: hello = hello-v0
    3-100: subdir/
    9-300: extra = extra-v0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    5-100: hello = hello-v0
    5-100: hello2
    3-100: subdir/
      7-100: inner = inner-v1
